Usage: cloudburrow trust [flags]

List the files up would act on without your naming them, ./cloudburrow.json and
the scripts in the default .cloudburrow/hooks (or a hooksDir the discovered file
sets), and record that you trust them as they are now. The record is a hash in
trust.json in the state directory; a change to any of them asks again.

Flags:
  -accept-mssql-eula
    	accept Microsoft's End-User Licensing Agreement for SQL Server (https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?LinkId=746388) yourself, for the Cloud SQL for SQL Server instances this instance creates: their servers run Microsoft's SQL Server image, which starts only once it is accepted; who accepted and when is recorded on each instance (also CLOUDBURROW_ACCEPT_MSSQL_EULA=Y)
  -allow-remote
    	permit binding a non-loopback address (unsafe)
  -appengine-url string
    	base URL of a local HTTP server standing in for the App Engine app, such as http://localhost:8080: Cloud Tasks and Cloud Scheduler deliver App Engine targets there (default: none, and every App Engine attempt fails 404)
  -artifact-registry-cleanup-interval duration
    	how often Artifact Registry's cleanup policies run (default 24h, about daily as Google's)
  -bigquery-heap-mib int
    	GOMEMLIMIT, in MiB, of the BigQuery emulator, which also sizes its container's memory request; a soft limit, past which it collects more often; 0 = none (default 512)
  -bind-address string
    	IP address to publish host endpoints on
  -cloudbuild-host-steps
    	let Cloud Build run steps other than docker build, docker push and pack, for builds submitted from this machine's loopback only; each runs as a container with the host's Docker socket, which gives it control of the host (unsafe)
  -cloudsql-connector string
    	host:port the Cloud SQL connectors' TLS listener binds; they dial port 3307, so a second instance takes another loopback address (default: bind address, port 3307)
  -cluster-provider string
    	cluster provider (only kind is supported)
  -config string
    	path to a JSON configuration file
  -cors-allow-origin value
    	web origin (scheme://host[:port]) whose browser requests Cloud Storage and every other listener answer, beyond loopback ones; repeatable or comma-separated (default: loopback origins only)
  -emulator-heap-mib int
    	maximum Java heap, in MiB, of the Pub/Sub, Firestore and Datastore emulators, which also sizes their containers' memory limit; 0 = unbounded (default 1024)
  -hook-env string
    	comma-separated variables of this environment passed to hooks beyond PATH, HOME, LANG, TMPDIR and the like
  -hook-timeout duration
    	time limit for each hook script (default 5m)
  -hooks-dir string
    	directory of ready.d and shutdown.d hook scripts (default .cloudburrow/hooks)
  -iam-enforcement string
    	IAM enforcement: off (policies are stored, never checked) or on (mapped API methods check the caller's permissions, as on Google) (default off)
  -kubeconfig string
    	explicit kubeconfig path (never the developer default)
  -local-ai-alias string
    	comma-separated model IDs that resolve to the configured model (explicit substitution)
  -local-ai-embeddings
    	serve text-embedding :predict for embeddinggemma-300m-onnx-community, a community ONNX conversion that is NOT an official Google artifact (needs a -tags onnx build)
  -local-ai-image string
    	local AI runtime image (default: the image published with this release; for a dev build, the one make litert-lm builds)
  -local-ai-model string
    	host path to a .litertlm model; enables the local generation endpoint
  -local-ai-model-id string
    	model ID clients must request (default: the catalogue entry for the artifact)
  -log-level string
    	log level: trace, debug, info, warn, error
  -mode string
    	state mode: ephemeral or persistent
  -name string
    	instance name; scopes the cluster, namespace and every owned resource
  -namespace string
    	namespace for CloudBurrow-managed workloads
  -node-image string
    	pinned kind node image, which fixes the Kubernetes version
  -port-analyticshub int
    	BigQuery sharing (Analytics Hub) API host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9042)
  -port-apikeys int
    	API Keys API (apikeys.googleapis.com) host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9029)
  -port-backupdr int
    	Backup and DR Service API host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9024)
  -port-base int
    	move every fixed default port so the layout starts here (control here, ingress +80, console +90); explicit --port-* flags still win (0 = the defaults, from 9000)
  -port-bigquery int
    	BigQuery emulator REST host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9014)
  -port-bigquery-storage int
    	BigQuery Storage Read API gRPC host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9015)
  -port-bigtable int
    	Bigtable emulator host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9012)
  -port-cloudsql int
    	Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9019)
  -port-cloudsql-mysql int
    	Cloud SQL for MySQL host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9017)
  -port-compute int
    	Compute Engine API (VPC networking) host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9031)
  -port-console int
    	host port for the web console (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-control int
    	control port for health, readiness and admin (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-datastore int
    	Datastore emulator host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9011)
  -port-datatransfer int
    	BigQuery Data Transfer Service host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9034)
  -port-firestore int
    	Firestore emulator host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9010)
  -port-firestore-mongodb int
    	Firestore with MongoDB compatibility host port, the MongoDB wire protocol (0 = OS-assigned; default 9026)
  -port-gke int
    	Kubernetes Engine API host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9030)
  -port-ingress int
    	host port for the cluster ingress gateway (0 = OS-assigned; fixed at cluster creation)
  -port-kms int
    	Cloud KMS host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9018)
  -port-localai int
    	host port for the local generation endpoint (0 = OS-assigned; requires -local-ai-model)
  -port-logging int
    	Cloud Logging host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9009)
  -port-memorystore int
    	Memorystore (Valkey, RESP) host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9016)
  -port-memorystore-admin int
    	Memorystore admin API (redis.googleapis.com) host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9021)
  -port-metadata int
    	host port for the local metadata server (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-monitoring int
    	Cloud Monitoring API host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9033)
  -port-onnx int
    	ONNX runner host port, for BigQuery ML's imported ONNX models in the onnx build (0 = OS-assigned; default 9025)
  -port-privateca int
    	Certificate Authority Service API host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9028)
  -port-pubsub int
    	Pub/Sub host port (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-resourcemanager int
    	Resource Manager v3 Projects API host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9007)
  -port-run int
    	Cloud Run host port (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-scheduler int
    	Cloud Scheduler host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9008)
  -port-secrets int
    	Secret Manager host port (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-serviceusage int
    	Service Usage API (serviceusage.googleapis.com) host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9023)
  -port-spanner int
    	Spanner emulator host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9013)
  -port-spanner-rest int
    	Spanner emulator REST API host port, which Terraform uses (0 = OS-assigned; default 9022)
  -port-sqladmin int
    	Cloud SQL Admin API host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9020)
  -port-storage int
    	Cloud Storage host port (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-storagebatchoperations int
    	Storage Batch Operations API (storagebatchoperations.googleapis.com) host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9035)
  -port-storageinsights int
    	Storage Insights API (storageinsights.googleapis.com) host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9036)
  -port-storagetransfer int
    	Storage Transfer Service API (storagetransfer.googleapis.com) host port (0 = OS-assigned; default 9037)
  -port-tasks int
    	Cloud Tasks host port (0 = OS-assigned)
  -port-tfconvert int
    	TensorFlow SavedModel converter host port, for BigQuery ML's imported TENSORFLOW models (0 = OS-assigned; default 9027)
  -project string
    	default project ID (default: the instance name when it is a valid project ID, otherwise derived from it)
  -ready-timeout duration
    	bounded time to wait for cluster components to become ready
  -seed-file string
    	seed document (the /admin/seed body) applied when up starts
  -services string
    	comma-separated services to start (default storage,pubsub,tasks,run,secretmanager; opt-in: firestore,datastore,bigtable,spanner,cloudsql,bigquery,memorystore,cloudsql-mysql,scheduler,logging,kms,backupdr,privateca,gke,monitoring,compute)
  -shutdown-timeout duration
    	bounded time to drain on shutdown
  -state-dir string
    	host directory for the generated kubeconfig and other artifacts
